# A thread of the OS server overflows its stack on purpose while it holds
# the server's lock (roadmap memory.md M6, D10's rule; tests/posix/
# overflow.c): the tables may be half changed, so the server's policy asks
# the root to stop the system (ROOT_PANIC), which it does with its own
# fault (D8).
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_OVERFLOW
define: TEST_OS_OVERFLOW_LOCKED
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
# DOSBox-X checks no stack segment's limit (docs/emulators.md): there the
# overflow faults at the segment's end instead (#GP), to the same end.
match: contains
timeout: 60
---
rx286: os: thread 19 faulted holding the lock: the system stops
rx286: root: thread 19 of os cannot go on: the system stops
rx286 PANIC: the root faulted
